  * Wine's desktop and the Linux programs' windows take turns in front.
    Every Wine window (File Explorer, Notepad, the Start menu) is inside
    Wine's desktop window, below a Linux program's (SG Office's editors),
    which hid them all: the Start menu opened behind SG Office. A new
    control command XDESKTOP (session_x11.c) puts the desktop in front,
    with the focus; the taskbar asks for it when a Wine window comes
    forward (wine-sg 0700). XACTIVATE also restacks X as the screen.
  * A Linux program bringing its own window forward (_NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW:
    SG Office when a file open in it is opened again) gets it in front.
  * A window moved by dragging its own title bar (_NET_WM_MOVERESIZE)
    stays where it was put: its next resize no longer centres it again.
  * Gates test-desktopfront and test-selfmove (mutants
    SG_MUTANT_DESKTOP_NOT_RAISED, SG_MUTANT_NO_SESSION_ACTIVATE,
    SG_MUTANT_GRAB_NOT_PLACED each fail them).
  * sg-deskcomp (/usr/libexec/stained-glass): the Wine desktop's own
    compositor. David: "The apps need to have drop shadows like in windows.
    We also should support alpha in windows." Every Windows program's
    window is an X child of Wine's desktop window, which X never blends;
    sg-deskcomp redirects them (Composite) and paints them into an
    input-transparent canvas over the desktop's picture (wine-sg 0744):
    real alpha (layered and per-pixel), drop shadows in the look's manner
    (_SG_SHADOW), and effects off by default: fade or zoom on open and
    close, a lamp or scale into the taskbar on minimize, wobbly windows,
    translucent while moved ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME/stained-glass/effects.conf,
    Settings writes it). Input is untouched; if it exits, X draws the
    desktop as before. Test: make test-deskcomp (pixels and frame dumps;
    mutants NOSHADOWS, OPAQUE, NOEFFECTS).
  * sg-deskcomp's wobble is drawn nearest-sampled at 30 frames a second: the
    bilinear mesh cost Xwayland about 60% of a core during a drag on the QA
    VM, this about 20% (a4e3c9a, whose changelog line this is).
  * sg-deskcomp: frosted windows. A window marked _SG_ACRYLIC (wine-sg 0745:
    the taskbar while "Transparency effects" is on) has what is below it
    blurred (an eighth of its size and back) and is laid over that,
    see-through by the rest; any change below repaints it whole. Test:
    deskcomp-gate (half see-through, blurred across an edge; mutant
    NOFROST).
  * sg-deskcomp leaves a full-screen window to X: when the window on top
    covers the desktop and is opaque and still (a game, a video), the
    canvas is hidden and that window is no longer redirected, so it costs
    no copy; another window above it, or a change of size, and it is
    composited again. Test: deskcomp-gate (direct=, the canvas unmapped,
    then back; mutant NODIRECT).

